<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan T$15 bln 91-day T-bills yield avg 6.882 pct.</title>
<headline>Taiwan T$15 bln 91-day T-bills yield avg 6.882 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's central bank, on behalf of the finance ministry, auctioned T$15 billion in 91-day treasury bills at an average yield of 6.882 percent, a central bank official said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>Demand totalled T$13.15 billion, marking one of the rare instances that demand fell below planned auction amount, the official said.</p>
<p>The actual value auctioned was T$11.85 billion.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
